new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ae43571
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.lore/dod.md
@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@
+# Definition of Done
+
+> `ToolRegistry.execute` looks a tool up, logs the input's key names, and calls the executor
+> without ever checking the declared `inputSchema` (`src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts`).
+> Every tool declares a JSON Schema (`src/types/ai.ts`) that is handed verbatim to both
+> providers, but nothing validates what comes back from the model.
+
+**Strategy: `direct`** — `ToolRegistry.register`, `ToolRegistry.execute` and `createChatOrchestrator` already expose the exact entry points this ticket changes, so the acceptance tests call them directly today and fail because schema compilation and input validation are absent.
+
+## Done when these pass
+
+- [ ] **rejects input missing a required property with a ToolResponse and never calls the executor** — `ToolRegistry.execute` validates `input` against `inputSchema`, returns a `ToolResponse` naming the missing required property, and does not invoke the executor.
+      `src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts`
+
+- [ ] **rejects a wrong-typed property naming the field and expected type without leaking the offending value to the result or logs** — `ToolRegistry.execute` rejects a property with the wrong JSON Schema type without calling the executor, names the failing field path and expected type in `result`, and omits the offending property value from both `result` and emitted log lines.
+      `src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts`
+
+- [ ] **throws at register time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled** — `ToolRegistry.register` compiles a static `ToolDefinition`'s `inputSchema` once at registration time and throws synchronously naming the tool when the schema is invalid.
+      `src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts`
+
+- [ ] **returns a schema rejection as a tool_result in the orchestrator loop so the model can correct the call on the next round** — `createChatOrchestrator` feeds a schema-rejected tool call's `ToolResponse.result` back to the provider as a `tool_result` without invoking the executor on the invalid call, allowing the model to retry with valid arguments and complete the turn.
+      `src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts`
+
+## Facets
+
+- [x] Repair CI-reported legacy Ajv option types, dynamic-cache constructor typing, enum test member chain, and rejection field paths.
+
+- [x] Name enum constraints in rejection feedback and repair CI-reported Ajv subpath type imports in the registry and its fixtures.
+
+- [x] Repair CI-reported v6 Ajv type resolution by using explicit v8 type declarations while preserving the runtime package-root import; consolidate the package-root fixture assertion.
+
+- [x] Repair CI-reported missing Ajv subpath resolution by loading runtime and types from the public package root.
+
+- [x] Repair CI-reported named Ajv import failures with the default constructor export and consolidate the valid-input assertion to satisfy lint.
+
+- [x] Repair the CI-reported Ajv constructor import and pin valid-input execution with an ESM export fixture.
+
+- [x] Compile a function-valued definition’s current schema at execute time, naming the tool on compilation failure.
+- [x] Repair the reported Ajv ESM import and acceptance-fixture lint findings.
+- [ ] Investigate the providerFactory VertexAI CI failure when CI supplies its missing error message (the current log tail contains only the stack).
+
+- [x] Reject uncompilable static input schemas at registration, naming the tool.
+
+- [x] Add `ajv` to `dependencies` in `package.json` and `package-lock.json` (`strict: false`, `validateFormats: false`, no coercion, no defaults, no injected `additionalProperties: false`) and bump the package version `MINOR`.
+- [x] Compile static `ToolDefinition.inputSchema` at registration and reuse the stored validator across executions without reading the schema again.
+- [x] Cache compiled validators for function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` schemas by schema object reference (`WeakMap`).
+- [x] Repair CI-reported Ajv type and rejection-path failures by importing the v8 entry point, and repair the rejection test’s vague name and member chain.
+- [x] Validate `input` in `ToolRegistry.execute` before invoking the executor, returning a `ToolResponse` (`{result}`) that names failing field paths and expected types/required fields without echoing or logging offending values, and add the one-line doc comment pointing at `specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md`.
+- [ ] Add unit tests in `src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts` and `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts`, link the remaining statements in `specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md`, and update `example/weather-tool.ts`, `docs/adding-a-tool.md`, `README.md`, `.specify/spec.md`, `adrs/ADR-002-response-validation.md`, and `CHANGELOG.md`.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- Output validation and domain sanity checks (covered by ADR-002), MCP tool-server discovery and proxying (#42), per-tool authorization or `beforeToolCall` hooks (#40), retry/timeout/rate-limiting around tool execution, and concrete tool implementations.
diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index fa1a2d5..6f745a0 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -8,6 +8,27 @@ package, not for somebody reading this repository's commit log.
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Changed
+
+- Tool rejection feedback preserves field paths when a legacy Ajv validator supplies errors.
+
+- Tool input rejections explicitly identify the failed schema constraint, including enum choices, without returning rejected values.
+
+- Dynamic tool schemas reuse validators by schema object identity.
+
+- Tool validation loads Ajv through its public package entry point for compatibility with dependency resolvers.
+
+- Static tool schemas are compiled at registration and the validator is reused on subsequent calls.
+
+- Tool executors now receive only input accepted by their declared JSON Schema. Invalid input returns a tool result to the model for correction; executors that previously produced their own malformed-input errors no longer see those calls. Extra properties pass through unchanged.
+
+- Tool schema compilation supports Ajv environments that expose only a default constructor export.
+
+- Tool registry initialization supports the Ajv constructor export without requiring a nested default export.
+
+- Function-valued tool definitions now reject an invalid current schema before their executor runs.
+- Registering a static tool now rejects an invalid JSON Schema immediately with an error naming the tool.
+
