diff --git a/specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md b/specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..472113c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/specs/hal-engine-tool-input-validation/spec.md
@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+Every tool registered in `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` that is forwarded to the configured AI provider, and `ToolRegistry.execute` validates the model-supplied `input` against that schema before calling the tool's executor. When validation fails, `execute` returns a rejection `ToolResponse` describing what was wrong rather than throwing, so the orchestrator feeds the failure back to the model as a `tool_result` within the existing tool-round budget.
+
+## Validation at execute time
+
+- When `input` omits a property listed in `required`, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the missing property as required and never invokes the executor ([validated by: rejects input missing a required property with a ToolResponse and never calls the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L16), [validated by: rejects malformed weather input before execution without exposing its value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry-input-validation.test.ts#L6)).
+- When `input` supplies a property whose value does not match its declared JSON Schema type, `ToolRegistry.execute` returns a `ToolResponse` naming the failing field path and expected type without invoking the executor, and neither `result` nor the emitted log record contains the offending property value ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed property naming the field and expected type without leaking the offending value to the result or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L46), [validated by: rejects malformed weather input before execution without exposing its value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry-input-validation.test.ts#L6)).
+- When `input` satisfies `required`, declared property types and `enum`, `ToolRegistry.execute` invokes the executor once and passes the input object through unchanged — including undeclared extra properties — without injecting `additionalProperties: false`, coercing types or applying defaults ([validated by: executes valid weather input once without changing extra properties or applying defaults](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry-valid-input.test.ts#L5)).
+- When `ToolRegistry.execute` is called with a tool name that has not been registered, it throws `Unknown tool: <name>` because an unregistered tool is a programming or configuration error rather than a recoverable input mistake.
+
+## Schema compilation and caching
+
+- A static `ToolDefinition` has its `inputSchema` compiled once at `register` time, so a schema that is not valid JSON Schema throws synchronously from `register` with an error message naming the offending tool ([validated by: rejects a static schema with an invalid type at registration](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L4), [validated by: throws at register time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L94)).
+- A static tool's `inputSchema` is compiled at `register` time and reused on every `execute` call without re-reading or re-compiling `definition.inputSchema` ([validated by: reuses the registered static schema across ten executions](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry-static-cache.test.ts#L5)).
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves its definition on each `execute` call and validates against the `inputSchema` returned for that call, caching compiled validators by schema object reference (`WeakMap`) so distinct returned schemas each enforce their own rules ([validated by: caches dynamic weather schemas by object identity](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry-dynamic-cache.test.ts#L7)).
+
+- A function-valued definition whose current schema is invalid fails compilation at execute time with an error naming the tool ([validated by: rejects an invalid current dynamic schema before executing weather](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.test.ts#L16)).
+
+## Orchestrator tool-loop recovery
+
+- Because a schema rejection returns a `ToolResponse` instead of throwing, `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` sends the rejection `result` back to the provider as a `tool_result` message, allowing the model to issue a corrected tool call on the next round and complete the turn within `maxToolRounds` ([validated by: returns a schema rejection as a tool_result in the orchestrator loop so the model can correct the call on the next round](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L112)).
+
+- The registry executes valid input with a default-only Ajv constructor export ([validated by: executes valid input with the default-only Ajv constructor export](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry-ajv.test.ts#L9)).
+
+- The registry loads the validator through the Ajv package root export ([validated by: constructs the weather validator through the Ajv package root](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry-ajv-root.test.ts#L19)).
+
+- Enum rejections name the field path and the enum constraint without returning the rejected value ([validated by: names the enum constraint when rejecting weather units](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry-enum.test.ts#L5)).
+
+- Rejections preserve field paths from legacy Ajv dataPath errors without exposing rejected values ([validated by: names legacy validator field paths without exposing weather input](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry-legacy-path.test.ts#L15)).
